# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows. A CRLF here breaks the
# shebang for anything that runs them on Linux - the kernel looks for an interpreter named
# "/bin/sh\r" and reports "not found" - which is what a Docker build does with the working tree.
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf

# Their Windows counterparts need the opposite
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touched by line-ending conversion
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
